{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-john-004",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 4,
  "title": "John 4",
  "display_title": "John 4",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "john",
  "book": "John",
  "bookName": "John",
  "bookOrder": 43,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 4,
  "sortOrder": 43004,
  "verseCount": 54,
  "aliases": [
    "John",
    "Jn",
    "Jhn"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "When therefore the LORD knew how the Pharisees had heard that Jesus made and baptized more disciples than John,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "(Though Jesus himself baptized not, but his disciples,)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "He left Judaea, and departed again into Galilee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And he must needs go through Samaria.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Then cometh he to a city of Samaria, which is called Sychar, near to the parcel of ground that Jacob gave to his son Joseph.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Now Jacob’s well was there. Jesus therefore, being wearied with his journey, sat thus on the well: and it was about the sixth hour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "There cometh a woman of Samaria to draw water: Jesus saith unto her, Give me to drink.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "(For his disciples were gone away unto the city to buy meat.)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Then saith the woman of Samaria unto him, How is it that thou, being a Jew, askest drink of me, which am a woman of Samaria? for the Jews have no dealings with the Samaritans.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Jesus answered and said unto her, If thou knewest the gift of God, and who it is that saith to thee, Give me to drink; thou wouldest have asked of him, and he would have given thee living water.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "The woman saith unto him, Sir, thou hast nothing to draw with, and the well is deep: from whence then hast thou that living water?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Art thou greater than our father Jacob, which gave us the well, and drank thereof himself, and his children, and his cattle?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Jesus answered and said unto her, Whosoever drinketh of this water shall thirst again:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "The woman saith unto him, Sir, give me this water, that I thirst not, neither come hither to draw.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Jesus saith unto her, Go, call thy husband, and come hither.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "The woman answered and said, I have no husband. Jesus said unto her, Thou hast well said, I have no husband:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "For thou hast had five husbands; and he whom thou now hast is not thy husband: in that saidst thou truly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The woman saith unto him, Sir, I perceive that thou art a prophet.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Our fathers worshipped in this mountain; and ye say, that in Jerusalem is the place where men ought to worship.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Jesus saith unto her, Woman, believe me, the hour cometh, when ye shall neither in this mountain, nor yet at Jerusalem, worship the Father.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Ye worship ye know not what: we know what we worship: for salvation is of the Jews.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "But the hour cometh, and now is, when the true worshippers shall worship the Father in spirit and in truth: for the Father seeketh such to worship him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship him in spirit and in truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "The woman saith unto him, I know that Messias cometh, which is called Christ: when he is come, he will tell us all things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Jesus saith unto her, I that speak unto thee am he.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "And upon this came his disciples, and marvelled that he talked with the woman: yet no man said, What seekest thou? or, Why talkest thou with her?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "The woman then left her waterpot, and went her way into the city, and saith to the men,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Come, see a man, which told me all things that ever I did: is not this the Christ?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Then they went out of the city, and came unto him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "In the mean while his disciples prayed him, saying, Master, eat.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "But he said unto them, I have meat to eat that ye know not of.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Therefore said the disciples one to another, Hath any man brought him ought to eat?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Jesus saith unto them, My meat is to do the will of him that sent me, and to finish his work.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "Say not ye, There are yet four months, and then cometh harvest? behold, I say unto you, Lift up your eyes, and look on the fields; for they are white already to harvest.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "And he that reapeth receiveth wages, and gathereth fruit unto life eternal: that both he that soweth and he that reapeth may rejoice together.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "And herein is that saying true, One soweth, and another reapeth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "I sent you to reap that whereon ye bestowed no labour: other men laboured, and ye are entered into their labours.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "And many of the Samaritans of that city believed on him for the saying of the woman, which testified, He told me all that ever I did.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-040",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 40,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:40",
      "numberLabel": "40",
      "text": "So when the Samaritans were come unto him, they besought him that he would tarry with them: and he abode there two days.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:40",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:40"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-041",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 41,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:41",
      "numberLabel": "41",
      "text": "And many more believed because of his own word;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:41",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-042",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 42,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:42",
      "numberLabel": "42",
      "text": "And said unto the woman, Now we believe, not because of thy saying: for we have heard him ourselves, and know that this is indeed the Christ, the Saviour of the world.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:42",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:42"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-043",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 43,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:43",
      "numberLabel": "43",
      "text": "Now after two days he departed thence, and went into Galilee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:43",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-044",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 44,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:44",
      "numberLabel": "44",
      "text": "For Jesus himself testified, that a prophet hath no honour in his own country.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:44",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:44"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-045",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 45,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:45",
      "numberLabel": "45",
      "text": "Then when he was come into Galilee, the Galilaeans received him, having seen all the things that he did at Jerusalem at the feast: for they also went unto the feast.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:45",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:45"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-046",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 46,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:46",
      "numberLabel": "46",
      "text": "So Jesus came again into Cana of Galilee, where he made the water wine. And there was a certain nobleman, whose son was sick at Capernaum.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:46",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:46"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-047",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 47,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:47",
      "numberLabel": "47",
      "text": "When he heard that Jesus was come out of Judaea into Galilee, he went unto him, and besought him that he would come down, and heal his son: for he was at the point of death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:47",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:47"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-048",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 48,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:48",
      "numberLabel": "48",
      "text": "Then said Jesus unto him, Except ye see signs and wonders, ye will not believe.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:48",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-049",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 49,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:49",
      "numberLabel": "49",
      "text": "The nobleman saith unto him, Sir, come down ere my child die.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:49",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:49"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-050",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 50,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:50",
      "numberLabel": "50",
      "text": "Jesus saith unto him, Go thy way; thy son liveth. And the man believed the word that Jesus had spoken unto him, and he went his way.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:50",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:50"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-051",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 51,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:51",
      "numberLabel": "51",
      "text": "And as he was now going down, his servants met him, and told him, saying, Thy son liveth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:51",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-052",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 52,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:52",
      "numberLabel": "52",
      "text": "Then enquired he of them the hour when he began to amend. And they said unto him, Yesterday at the seventh hour the fever left him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:52",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:52"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-053",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 53,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:53",
      "numberLabel": "53",
      "text": "So the father knew that it was at the same hour, in the which Jesus said unto him, Thy son liveth: and himself believed, and his whole house.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:53",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-054",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 54,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:4:54",
      "numberLabel": "54",
      "text": "This is again the second miracle that Jesus did, when he was come out of Judaea into Galilee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 4:54",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:4:54"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "repository": "aruljohn/Bible-kjv",
